 "_prompt": "You are matching code-review findings against a known bug. Reply with ONLY a JSON object.\n\nKNOWN BUG: When the target is itself a shadow host, its own shadow content is hidden.\n\nRules:\n- Answer \"yes\" only if the text describes THIS specific bug: the same faulty behaviour in the same situation. A finding about a nearby but different behaviour (another header, another edge case, a different race) is \"no\".\n- A finding that says the behaviour was checked and PASSED, or that the code handles it correctly, is \"no\".\n- Wording does not matter; the behaviour does.\n- For handoffs: count only text that tells the implementor to fix this bug (a reported finding, a fix instruction). Restated acceptance criteria that merely describe the desired behaviour do NOT count as carrying the finding unless the handoff ties them to a reported failure.\n\n=== REVIEW 1 FINDINGS ===\n- [blocking] Slotted target is hidden by its flat-tree ancestor. Light child `<button id=\"q5t\">` of host `div`; shadow root is `<i id=\"sib\"></i><slot id=\"sl\"></slot>`; after `ariaHideOutside([t])`, `sl` has `aria-hidden=\"true\"`, so the target sits under an aria-hidden node. Cause: `getEnclosingShadowRoots` and the walk follow DOM parents and host chains, not slot assignment, so the slot's shadow-root wrapper is not treated as containing the target. Same with a wrapper `<section><slot/></section>` (Q1). Violates \"targets stay visible\".\n- [minor] Slot-hosting root is not observed. In Q6, content appended later to the shadow root that holds the `<slot>` (a flat-tree ancestor of the slotted target) is not hidden. The spec's \"light-DOM-like\" allowance covers the slot case, so I rate it minor.\n- [minor] Target reached only via a slot (Q2): the target's host `hb` and wrapper `sec` in the outer root are aria-hidden, which hides the target. This is the allowed light-DOM-like class and does not throw.\n- [minor] `querySelectorAllInShadowRoots` runs a full `querySelectorAll('*')` plus recursion on every added node in the observer, so cost is O(page) per mutation. Not reproduced as a failure; performance only.\n- [minor] Pre-existing, not in the diff: a second `revert()` on a non-top call runs `splice(indexOf(...) = -1, 1)`, which removes the last stack entry. Visible at HEAD line 208; not reproduced here.\n- [minor] Flag-off tests live in the same file as flag-on tests and depend on declaration order (enableShadowDOM is global and cannot be reset). Works under the current order, but is fragile.\n- [minor] Two overlapping calls where the second target is inside an element the first call already hid (sibling-host case) keep the target hidden until the first call restores. This matches existing light-DOM behaviour, so it is not shadow-specific.\n=== REVIEW 2 FINDINGS ===\n- [minor] Criterion 7 (`shouldUseInert` in shadow roots) is only covered by a test that depends on `jest.isolateModules` plus a manual `inert` property on `HTMLElement.prototype`. The file's flag-off tests also rely on running before the `enableShadowDOM` beforeAll. This is correct today, but it is order-dependent. Not reproduced as a failure.\n- [minor] Late content added to a shadow root that is not on any target's flat path (for example a named-slot shadow root that an unslotted light child of a path host sits in) is not observed. Not reproduced as a visible problem: the content is unrendered or sits under an already-hidden host.\n- [minor] `handledHosts` and the per-call sets are never pruned, so they can keep references to removed hosts until the call is reverted. Not reproduced as a leak in practice.\n- Round-1 items re-checked and now passing: Q5 (slot not hidden, sibling hidden), Q1 (section wrapping slot not hidden), Q6 (late content in slot-hosting shadow root hidden), Q2 (path hosts visible through an outer slot).\n=== IMPLEMENTOR HANDOFF 1 (sent after review 1) ===\nRepo: /tmp/ff-eval-8srvvqip/workspace. Fix round 1 for the shadow DOM support in packages/@react-aria/overlays/src/ariaHideOutside.ts (see `git diff packages/@react-aria/overlays`). Don't touch yarn.lock, package.json, FEATURE_FLOW.md, or packages/@react-aria/utils.\n\nGOAL: With the flag on, a target that is slotted (a light-DOM child of a shadow host, rendered through a <slot> in that host's shadow root) must never end up under an aria-hidden/inert ancestor in the flat tree, and the shadow roots that hold those slots must be observed like other enclosing roots.\n\nReproduced blocking failures from the reviewer:\n- Q5: host `div` with light child `<button id=\"t\">` (the target); host's shadow root is `<i id=\"sib\"></i><slot id=\"sl\"></slot>`. After `ariaHideOutside([t])`, `sl` gets aria-hidden=\"true\" (target hidden). Expected: `sib` hidden, `sl` and host visible, t visible.\n- Q1: same, but the shadow root is `<i id=\"sib\"></i><section><slot></slot></section>` \u2192 section gets aria-hidden. Expected: section and slot visible, sib hidden.\n- Q6: content appended later to the shadow root holding the slot is not hidden. Expected: hidden (waitFor).\n- Q2 (also fix): target whose host chain is reached only through a slot in an outer shadow root \u2014 host and wrapper in the outer root got aria-hidden.\nCause: `nodeContains` from @react-aria/utils follows `assignedSlot` only for <slot> elements themselves, not for slotted elements, and `getEnclosingShadowRoots` follows only getRootNode().host.\n\nSuggested fix (gated on shadowDOM(); flag-off path unchanged): when the flag is on, compute for each target its flat-tree ancestor path: starting from the target, repeatedly go to `node.assignedSlot` if it is non-null (for Elements), else `parentNode`, and from a ShadowRoot go to `.host`; stop at `root` (or when null). Put every Element on the path into a `pathNodes` set and every ShadowRoot on the path into the observed `shadowRoots` list (stop collecting at root; don't include roots outside root's tree \u2014 keep the current rule that observation stops at root's own root node). Replace `getEnclosingShadowRoots` with this. In acceptNode, an Element in `pathNodes` returns FILTER_SKIP (before the \"contains a target\" loop). Keep the existing nodeContains loop for targets added later via keepVisible. Make sure the MutationObserver callback's \"is change.target inside a visible node\" check still makes sense: additions inside a slot-hosting root that isn't inside a target must get hidden; additions inside the target must not.\n\nAdd tests for Q5, Q1, Q6, Q2 in the shadow DOM describe of packages/@react-aria/overlays/test/ariaHideOutside.test.js (fail first, then fix). Also a test that a slotted light-DOM sibling of the target (another light child of the same host, assigned to the same or a different slot) is hidden.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:\n1. With the flag on, everything outside the targets is hidden, including siblings inside the targets' shadow roots and inside every shadow root that encloses them (nested shadow roots, at least 2 levels). The hosts on the path to a target are NOT hidden (no aria-hidden / inert on them).\n2. With the flag on, content added after the call anywhere in a target's shadow root or any shadow root enclosing it (including deeper inside an existing sibling subtree that is not hidden \u2014 e.g. a new child of a host on the path) gets hidden (asserted via waitFor). Content added inside a target stays visible.\n3. Live announcers (`data-live-announcer=\"true\"`) and top-layer elements (`data-react-aria-top-layer=\"true\"`) stay visible both when present at call time inside a shadow root and when added later inside a shadow root, as in the light DOM.\n4. Targets can live in different shadow roots (e.g. input in shadow root A, popover in shadow root B, or popover in light DOM body): both stay visible, their siblings in each root hidden, both hosts visible, and later additions in both roots get hidden.\n5. The returned function restores everything (all aria-hidden / inert removed from elements it set, including inside shadow roots) and stops observing all roots \u2014 content added after restore in any shadow root is not hidden.\n6. Nested calls (observerStack): an inner ariaHideOutside call pauses the outer's observation of shadow roots too, and restoring the inner one resumes observing the outer's shadow roots.\n7. `shouldUseInert: true` works the same in shadow roots.\n8. With the flag off, nothing changes; all existing ariaHideOutside tests pass unchanged.\n9. Tests live in packages/@react-aria/overlays/test/ariaHideOutside.test.js. Caller tests still pass. `yarn eslint` and `yarn check-types` pass.\n\nCHECKS: while working `yarn jest packages/@react-aria/overlays/test/ariaHideOutside.test.js`; at the end `yarn jest packages/@react-aria/overlays packages/@react-aria/combobox packages/@react-aria/dialog packages/react-aria-components/test/Popover packages/react-aria-components/test/ComboBox`, `yarn eslint packages/@react-aria/overlays`, `yarn check-types`.\n\nReply exactly:\n{\"found\": \"yes\"|\"no\", \"review\": <review number or null>, \"finding_quote\": \"<verbatim quote of the finding, or empty>\",\n  \"sent\": \"yes\"|\"no\", \"handoff\": <handoff number or null>, \"handoff_quote\": \"<verbatim quote from the handoff, or empty>\"}\n\"sent\" can be \"yes\" only if \"found\" is \"yes\" and the handoff came after that review."
